cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "cassnoccurrences: CASSN Occurrence Dataset Pipeline"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-02
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23897764
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/john-imperato/cassn-occurrences"
abstract: >-
  R package that reads conventionally staged Wildlife Insights, NABat or SonoBat,
  Motus, and California Sentinel Sites for Nature (CASSN) ingest metadata, applies
  consistent occurrence rules, and writes one standardized comma-separated
  occurrence dataset with a build receipt.
authors:
  - family-names: Imperato
    given-names: John
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-7043-8937"
    affiliation: "University of California Natural Reserve System, UC Davis"
keywords:
  - biodiversity
  - occurrence records
  - camera traps
  - passive acoustic monitoring
  - Motus
  - Wildlife Insights
  - NABat
  - data harmonization
